WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.616 --> 00:00:09.750
MARKUS KLUTE: Welcome
back to 8.701.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:13.020
So in this lecture, we want to
talk about asymptotic freedom,

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.980
about confinement, and also
the running of the strength

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.700
of the strong force.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.470
In the recitation,
we already talked

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:27.090
about vacuum polarization,
QED, and how it relates to QCD.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.790
So here we're just going
to remind ourselves again

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.080
about what has been
discussed here.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.530
So loop contributions
in QED, they

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:37.710
make the effective charge
a function of the momentum

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:38.820
transferred q.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.610
So the coupling strength
increases with larger values

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.050
of q squared.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:46.410
So a leading order, you have
to consider this diagram.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:52.290
And you find that there
is a correction coming

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.280
from this kind of diagram.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.130
m here is the mass
of the particle

00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:00.400
involved in this correction.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.500
But as you know, in
perturbation theory,

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.540
you have to consider
all possible diagrams.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.100
And this is being done here.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.400
So if you consider those
higher-order diagrams,

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:14.290
you can rewrite the
running of the QED coupling

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:18.730
as the coupling at q
squared of 0 divided by 1

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:22.800
minus this contribution here.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.050
So there's a couple
of things to note.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:29.480
So there's a 1
minus a factor here.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.770
And then there's
also the definition

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:34.590
or the fixed point
of the coupling

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.990
that's being used
as 0 q squared.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.790
But that's possible in QED.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.160
But that will not
be possible in QCD,

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:44.370
because at momentum
transfer 0, the coupling

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.760
is going to be infinite.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:49.620
So it's not well-defined and we
cannot use perturbation theory

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.850
at this value s either.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.920
OK, good.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.130
So in QCD, we have
not just one diagram,

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.000
like the one we just saw before.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.870
But we also have to consider
the gluon self-coupling diagram.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:05.960
So we have contributions
of this sort.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:08.270
So I'll spare you
from the calculation.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:12.560
But you find that the
gluon contribution

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.870
has an opposite effect.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:20.060
So it's producing some sort of
anti-screening or camouflaging

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.410
of the color charge.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.030
And so you find,
if you calculate

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.340
this in a very similar way
as you did just before,

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.160
we did just before for QED, we
find this kind of correction.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:35.660
So here, we have
to define or fix

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.880
the strength of the coupling
at a specific scale.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.360
And you see that you have
this contribution here.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.400
There's a plus here,
but this factor here,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.270
which is 11 times the
number of colors involved,

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:50.270
minus 2 times the number
of flavors involved.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:55.370
Those numbers are 3 and
6, so hence 11 times

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.040
n is larger than 2 times f.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.900
This becomes positive here.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.310
And so therefore the
coupling decreases--

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:07.150
the coupling decreases
this q squared.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.475
All right, since
it decreases with q

00:03:09.475 --> 00:03:13.730
squared, at very,
very high q squared,

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.380
the coupling becomes 0.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.620
And that's the origin
of asymptotic freedom.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:23.850
In the limit of very
large q squared,

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.210
strongly charged particles,
color-charged particles

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:29.770
become free.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:34.360
That's also the reason
why at very high energies

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:38.320
we can make calculations in
QCD using the Feynman calculus

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.660
or perturbation theory.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:46.040
In the other direction, if
you go to very low q squared,

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.770
those methods and tools
are not possible anymore.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:52.020
And quarks and gluons
are actually confined.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:58.700
You cannot produce a non-color
thing that stays by themselves.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:06.020
You cannot have a free
gluon or free quark.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.790
So let's look at this
running a little bit more.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:13.820
So we have this annoying alpha
s over function of q squared.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:17.930
You can get rid of this actually
by redefining the parameter

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:21.320
here and using this lambda
parameter, or lambda QCD

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.690
as it's often called,
or lambda color

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:27.530
as it's called here under C.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.630
When we do this, we can
rewrite the equations.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.170
So we find that there
is no dependency anymore

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.430
of the scale involved.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:37.040
And we don't have to
find this fixed point.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.630
We still have the
dependency of 11n minus 2f.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.850
And then this locked
dependency on q

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:48.620
squared over this
specific scale.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.980
So the strength of the coupling
with this definition defined

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:55.370
for any value of q squared,
finding this lambda q,

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:58.470
this is kind of complicated
because if you go to very low q

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.740
square, calculations and
experiments cannot easily be

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.200
compared anymore.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:09.940
So we find that lambda QCD is
in the order of 100 to 500 MeV.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:16.150
OK, here are experimental
measurements, so alpha.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:19.090
The strength of the
strong interaction

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.220
has been measured
in many experiments.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.940
We can measure
this, for example,

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:26.170
in decays of tau leptons where
there's hadrons being produced,

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:30.940
and therefore you have
sensitivity to alpha s.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:34.900
You can use found states deep in
elastic scattering experiment.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:40.600
And PDF [?] fits can be used
in order to constrain alpha s.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:42.460
We can use e-plus
e-minus physics

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.350
and look at the
distribution of jets.

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:47.290
We saw that the additional
radiation of a gluon

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:52.660
is sensitive to this vertex
of a quark radiating a gluon,

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:57.670
and therefore to
the strength of QCD.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.230
You find that those
experiments are

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:00.850
all in reasonable agreement.

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:04.570
This line here indicates
now the average value

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:07.960
at a specific scale.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.300
And typically when people
compare measurements,

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:14.800
they use the scale of the
Z boson mass, about 90 GeV,

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.870
in order to compare the values.

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.720
And you can see here,
the running of alpha

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:23.725
s, the running of the strong
coupling, a function of q,

00:06:23.725 --> 00:06:26.380
and you see the behavior
of asymptotic freedom,

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:27.760
meaning that the
coupling becomes

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:31.900
small at very large value
of q, and very large--

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:35.060
small values of [INAUDIBLE].

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:39.170
All right, so that's it
for asymptotic freedom

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:42.360
and the running of alpha s.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.600
We have a little bit more
of a discussion in QCD

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.290
before we enter
the next chapter.

